The paper’s decisive split is clear. Searching for arbitrary Beauville pairs is a poor family: Theorem 2.5 says that in the broad “nice power structure” regime every lift from the two-dimensional Frattini quotient works, so witnesses are abundant and efficiently constructed. I’m instead testing the paper’s native formal-power-series problem behind Corollary 3.4: compute a very high iterate in the Nottingham group. This is a plausible Track B family—the paper gives a short structural formula, while direct truncated-series iteration is exact but mechanically large.
