codex
Implemented the Track B Nottingham-series generator based on [arXiv:1507.02942](https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.02942).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/gen_1507_02942.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1507.02942/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

All local gates pass. Shipping measurements include:

- Exact answer density: \(10^{-16}\)
- Random guesses: 0/200,000
- Six attacks: 0/8 each
- Reference algorithm: 26,433,878 operations, 7.50 seconds
- Compact route: 136 operations
- Worst-case answer: 257 characters, 209 conservative tokens, 24 terms

The result is not yet shippable: OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” for every bare, hinted, and placebo attempt. Those errors are preserved and correctly count as zero valid oracle attempts—not as model failures. Replenish `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and rerun the three hardening arms to complete qualification.
