  1111	
  1112	
  1113	\begin{cor}
  1114	\label{p^mth_powers}
  1115	For every $\lambda\in\F_p$ and $m\ge 1$, we have
  1116	\[
  1117	f_{\lambda}^{p^m}(t) \equiv t+ (1-\lambda)^m t^{z_m}- (1- \lambda)^{m+1}t^{z_m+1} \pmod{t^{z_m+2}}.
  1118	\]
  1119	\end{cor}
  1120	
  1121	
  1122	
  1123	On several occasions, we will find ourselves working in a quotient of the form
  1124	$\No/\No_{z_m+1}$, which for simplicity we will call $G$.
  1125	In that case, we will systematically write $N_k$ for $\No_k/\No_{z_m+1}$, for
  1126	$1\le k\le z_m+1$, and $M_{\lambda}$ instead of $\MM_{\lambda}/\No_{z_m+1}$,
  1127	for every $\lambda\in\F_p$.
  1128	We will use this notation without further reference.
